    "name": "SF-503 - Remove Sub_Type__c from Lead (Non-Required) - API Tests",
    "description": "API - SF-503 - Remove Sub_Type__c from Lead page layout and make it non-required\n\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nGenerated: 2026-01-18\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nSUMMARY:\n  Remove Sub_Type__c from Lead page layout and make it non-required\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n  As a Product Owner / Sales Ops I want the Lead field Sub_Type__c removed from \n  the Lead page layout and ensured to be non-required So that users no longer \n  see the field when creating or editing Leads and the field is not enforced \n  as mandatory by the UI or automation.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n  1. Sub_Type__c field exists but is non-required\n  2. Leads can be created without Sub_Type__c (no validation errors)\n  3. Leads can be updated without Sub_Type__c\n  4. API/integrations accept requests without Sub_Type__c\n  5. Field is not visible on page layouts (UI test, not API)\n\nAPI TESTING REQUIREMENTS:\n  - Verify Sub_Type__c field exists on Lead\n  - Verify field is not required (required: false)\n  - Create Lead without Sub_Type__c (should succeed)\n  - Create Lead with Sub_Type__c (should succeed)\n  - Update Lead Sub_Type__c\n  - Query Lead by Sub_Type__c\n  - Handle null/blank Sub_Type__c values\n  - Reject invalid Sub_Type__c values (if picklist)\n\nGenerated from: src/features/api/SF/SF-503.feature\n\nThis collection contains API tests for SF-503 work item.\n\n**Note:** Sub_Type__c should exist but be non-required. Leads can be created/updated without this field.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
